Yes, Pestilence is difficult.  And my personal opinion is that adding 
the stunning attack on top of the illness one is unbalancing; also the 
wand of death misses often enough, so you cannot keep Pestilence away 
every time, which makes things a bit of a gambling, and this is an 
aspect that I don't like.  For spellcasters, things are not too bad, 
though, since they can almost always hit him with magic missiles 
sufficiently hard (the spell does not miss as often as the wand of 
death, I think).  But for combat wombats, which I have not played in 
ages in vanilla, I don't know.  If they can throw several daggers at 
once or use a bow very efficiently, they should prepare a few +7 daggers 
or (some more) +7 arrows.  If they can't, I guess, the best bet for them 
is to go to the two other altars first.

It is true that being killed by Pestilence is s.th. that cannot be 
avoided with certainty for some classes.  But then one should wear an 
amulet of life saving in that case (and a shield of reflection, if one 
cannot cast spells successfully anyway), which should always allow to 
take two swings at Pestilence, i.e. to kill him at least once.  If he 
does not resurrect too fast, that should be sufficient to get to the altar.

